From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] perf(canvas): keep live iframes only for frames near the
 camera

A page of a few hundred frames kept a few hundred live documents: every
frame laid out, rasterized and held in memory at once, so the editor
slowed down for every click (203 frames: ~590 ms click to paint in our
deployment). Frames far from the camera, or on screen while zoomed out
past reading (< 30%), now show their persisted preview image
(/i/<id>.jpg?preview) and get their iframe back when the camera comes
near. Selected frames and frames a peer or agent is editing always stay
live. The live set is computed by the Stage when the camera rests and
published per frame, so a pan re-renders only the frames that flip.

localStorage['doop:cull'] = 'off' restores the old behaviour.

Bench (tests/liveFramesBrowser.test.ts, 200 frames at 35%): live
iframes 200 -> 20, seed and settle 3.7 s -> 1.0 s, page heap
225 -> 86 MB, click to paint 40 -> 31 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
